# Official terms

Read `DEFINITIONS.md`. Do not invent synonyms.

| Official | Meaning | Code today |
|---|---|---|
| **Page** | The canvas | `conversations`, `/board/{id}` |
| **Frame** | Box holding text (one or more blocks) | RF `chatPanel`, `metadata.isBlock` |
| **Block** | TipTap line + ⋮⋮ | `EditorBlockRef`, `.tt-block-highlight` |
| **Thread** | Line between frames | RF `Edge`, `panel_edges` |
| **Connection point** | Knob that starts/receives a thread | RF `Handle` |

There is no “block group” product type — multiple blocks live in a **frame**. RF `blockGroup` is legacy wrapper chrome.

When the user says drag **this block** / the blue line / ⋮⋮, move that TipTap block only. Never start RF frame drag from ⋮⋮.

`metadata.isBlock` = this message is a **frame**, not a TipTap block.

Do not call a frame a card/panel/block. Do not call a thread an edge. Do not call a connection point a handle, nodule, or node. Do not call the page a board/map/canvas in new copy.
